Third-party content
-------------------

This distribution includes agent skills adapted from vendored third-party
material. Each adapted SKILL.md also carries a one-line provenance note, and
since 2026-07-29 a `license` field in its frontmatter naming the upstream.

Both exist because this file does not travel with a packaged skill. The
distribution unit is the skill directory, so anything at the repository root is
left behind by the installers, by `npx skills`, and by a `.skill` archive. The
body note is what a person reads; the frontmatter field is what a registry or a
packaging tool can inspect. Keep all of them in agreement.

Since 2026-08-06 (feat-0043) each adapted file also carries a machine-readable
provenance block naming the exact upstream file, its author, its license, the
date it was retrieved, and the SHA256 of the retrieved bytes. The block travels
with the file, so it survives packaging the way this NOTICE does not, and
`scripts/check-provenance.py` re-fetches every recorded source and reports drift.
The convention, including where the block lives in each file type and why the
digest is of the upstream bytes rather than of the adapted file, is in the
conventions section of AGENTS.md.

The blocks listed below were backfilled on 2026-08-06, well after the fold-ins
themselves. The vendored snapshot they were adapted from was gitignored and is
gone, so each digest pins upstream as of the backfill date rather than proving
the exact bytes originally adapted. That is the honest limit of a backfill, and
it is recorded in each block's note rather than left for a reader to infer.

